# ---
# title: tier / rung coherence — population
# description: >
#   Every claim the tier-rung-coherence gate could judge: a normative statement
#   carrying BOTH an rfc:tier and an au:rung. A claim with no TTL tier is
#   untiered, not Structural (rdf/ontology/tier.ttl), and is outside the gate's
#   reach by design — so over a corpus where nothing carries a tier this reads
#   EXAMINED_NOTHING, which is the truthful answer, not a pass.
# severity: error
# ---
# ⛔ AUTHORED, AND THAT IS THE RISK. Nothing mechanically proves this pattern is
# the gate's candidate set. If it drifts wider than the gate, a gate that
# examined nothing wears a large number and reads as thorough — strictly worse
# than silence. gate_cli refuses a population smaller than the violation count;
# that is a guard, not a proof. Review this file and its gate together or not at
# all.
PREFIX rfc: <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/rfc#>
PREFIX au:  <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/authoring#>
SELECT ?claim
WHERE {
  ?claim a rfc:NormativeStatement ; rfc:tier ?tier ; au:rung ?rung .
}
